# [Claude, 2026-10-29] Antidunes exploratory run configs/jobs not cited in the thesis (hundreds of
# .prm/.sbatch files accumulated across months of exploratory simulation work) -- kept on disk, just
# untracked going forward so they don't clutter the public GitHub view. The ~57 prms + ~27 sbatch
# files actually used by thesis-cited results are force-added (git add -f) and stay tracked despite
# these patterns. This does NOT scrub them from existing git history (see commit message).
apps/showcases/Antidunes/prms/*.prm
apps/showcases/Antidunes/jobs/*.sbatch
